WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.710
Ever since I can remember I had the
dream to start my own organic soap

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:09.690
company. That was the reason why I took
this job in the first place. But there I

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.070
was working in the marketing department
of a big brand as a junior administrator

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:19.470
and instead of being excited to work for
this famous company I was frustrated

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.480
about how things were handled. I felt
completely lonely with my ideas to make

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:31.140
a positive impact. I spent the entire
next weekend studying different pitch

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.280
formats. I figured that it would be best
to follow the requirements of one of the

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.000
big startup accelerators if I could
pitch to one of them I could certainly

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.530
pitch to the marketing director. I opted
for a pitch deck which is based on the

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:50.219
following six elements: the problem, my
solution, the business model, the market

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:59.010
the competition, our team. Okay so the
problem: well most body soap brands not

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.930
only lack a truly refreshing smell but
more importantly they also sell in cheap

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:09.030
throwaway plastic containers which often
lasts not more than a month. New modern

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:13.740
consumers however see body soap as a
lifestyle choice and they want to have a

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.960
solution that not only works but also
smells incredibly refreshing and is

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:26.250
environmentally friendly my solution I
call elements it's an organic soap which

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:32.220
comes in four fantastic flavors water
sky earth and fire in the first order

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:36.509
customers get all four flavors and a
beautiful glass jar and with a click of

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:40.560
a button they get refill packs sent to
their home in sustainable carton

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.159
packages

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:47.520
the business model is the result of our
understanding of the lifetime value of a

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:53.070
customer my customers will be very loyal
as they made a clear lifestyle choice to

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:58.289
buy it the first purchase someone makes
is therefore just seen as an investment

00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:03.659
we make into a long lasting relationship
it will cost customers 25 US dollars and

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:08.009
they get a beautiful glass jar and the
trial set of all four flavors the money

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:12.480
we make later from selling the refill
packs and sustainable paper bags for 15

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:19.739
US dollars similar to the famous razor
and blades business model the market is

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:25.650
enormous in the beginning we will target
urban women aged 20 to 30 years living

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.340
in the United States they are
well-educated they care about the

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.060
environment and are interested to
express themselves through lifestyle

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:38.880
choices based on my research they spent
on average around 50 to $100 on body

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.069
soap each year as there are around 15
million women in the US who are in their

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:49.709
20s living in urban areas the total
market opportunity is at least 750

00:02:49.709 --> 00:02:54.359
million dollars a year once we capture
some of that we will expand to other

00:02:54.359 --> 00:03:02.100
consumers and go global our competition
are big brands they own the market and

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.670
they've been telling consumers over the
years that body wash comes in a cheap

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:10.290
plastic bottle which ends up in the
ocean or on a landfill smaller startups

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.489
like ours might compete with them in
some segments but we rather consider

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:19.380
them as allies as we fight for the same
thing educating consumers to make a

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:25.980
switch to a more sustainable soap the
team that's me and my brother who

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.450
currently studies biochemistry but soon
he will have his degree and since he's a

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:35.670
real nature freak he is full on board to
help me develop a winning formula my

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:40.139
strengths are communication organization
and a clear understanding of what girls

00:03:40.139 --> 00:03:44.880
my age want it took me until Sunday
night until I had what I thought was the

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:50.610
perfect pitch
few days later in the office I saw the

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:54.420
marketing director and took the
initiative I asked him to give me three

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.140
minutes of his time so I could pitch to
him but instead of hearing me out he

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.129
just said why don't you pitch it next
Monday at the board meeting the old guys

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:05.970
are always open for new ideas from the
young people within the company maybe

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:10.470
they will fund a prototype and do a
market test then he added with a smile

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:17.310
the biggest secret of getting funding is
this ask for money you'll get advice ask

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:24.060
for advice and you'll get money I was
completely blown away I should present

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:31.530
my idea to the board and I knew exactly
what to ask for I couldn't sleep that

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:35.910
night I was too excited about what the
marketing director had told me the next

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:39.090
morning when I went through my pitch
again I wasn't sure if I was really

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:43.650
prepared I called my former teacher he
had already started several successful

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.620
companies
the next day we met and I pitched my

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:51.900
idea to him after he listened to me my
teacher got really excited and said if

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:57.470
they don't buy your idea on Monday I'll
offer to finance you to get started

00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:06.450
oMG I was so excited and so thankful on
my way home I reflected on my situation

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:11.160
I wondered if I really want to pitch to
the board and carry on working for the

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.780
same company which makes me feel
miserable after all I only worked there

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:20.760
to gain enough experience to start my
own business I realized that actually I

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:26.030
don't want someone else to buy and sell
my idea I want to try making it myself

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:32.370
it was clear to me that this is my
chance to finally get started I called

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:36.900
my manager thanked him for his time and
told him I'll quit my job to start my

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.110
own thing

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:43.530
how about you did you ever try to pitch
your business idea

